Review of e1a6415 (2026-11-25). The check was wired to `filepath.Join(setupState, "observe")`. On a joined device, `ohya setup` registers the MCP servers with `--state <state>/join` (cmd/ohya/setup.go), and `ohya doctor` without flags examines `<state>/join`. The snapshots of those servers were invisible to the check, so the one joined device of the owner (the MacBook) would never get the warning.

The regression test runs the doctor command for both layouts and prints nothing in the remote case before this commit. A test binary reports no build revision (`go test` stamps no VCS information), so `doctorRuntime.buildRevision` names the build to compare against; an empty value means this binary.

Not changed: the check compares the revision only, so a dirty build of the same revision is not reported.
